<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n83550" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλᾰτικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλάτος</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of</i> or <i>in latitude,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θέσεις, ἀπόστασις,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Procl.
				<u>Hyp.</u>
				5.6
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				8
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> metaph.,
				<i>broad, general,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. θεωρία,</span> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μοιρική,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Vett.Val.
				112.25
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. καὶ καθολικὴ θ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					289.15
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				243.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of meanings
			of words, <i>broad, wide,</i> or <i>involving breadth,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ κοινὸς καὶ π. τόπος</span>”
				<i>in the broad sense,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Simp.
					<u>in Ph.</u>
					637.24
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ νῦν, οὐ τὸ π. ἀλλὰ τὸ ἄτομον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>in Cael.</u>
					579.16
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ἐστιν ὁ ἐνεστώς: οἱονεὶ γὰρ
					πλάτος ὑπεμφαίνει ὡς πρὸς τὸν . . ἀκαριαῖον
					λεγόμενον χρόνον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Choerob.
					<u>in Theod.</u>
					2.12
				</span></i>
			 H. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>”
				<i>broadly speaking,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ach.Tat.
					<u>Intr.Arat.</u>
					18
				</span></i>
			, Vett. Val.<i><span class="en">
				274.34
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Simp.
				<u>in Cat.</u>
				426.23
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phlp.
				<u>in Cat.</u>
				46.19
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ἐξήγησις</span>
			<i>detailed</i> exegesis, <i><span class="en">
				Ammon.
				<u>in Porph.</u>
				60.6
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κωτέραν τὴν ἴασιν εὑρήσεις ἐν . .</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Paul.Aeg.
					2.25
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				Comp.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ώτερον, ἐξηγούμενος,</span> opp.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεφαλαιωδῶς,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				6.53
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
			</span></i> ad <i><span class="en">
				D.P.
				<u>Proll.</u>
				p.71
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				B.
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλατυκ-</span> is read in <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
			</span></i> l.c., and as v.l. in inferior codd. of <i><span class="en">
				Phlp.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ammon.
			</span></i> ll. cc., <i><span class="en">
				Simp.
				<u>in Cael.</u>
			</span></i> l.c., <i><span class="en">
				Paul.Aeg.
			</span></i> ll.cc.; cf. Lat. <i>platicus.</i>)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
